Third-party code
================

Verdant is MIT licensed; see LICENSE. This file records the code in or around
this repository that is somebody else's, so that the licence above is not read
as covering it.

It also records the two files whose SPDX header disagrees with that licence, and
why the header rather than the licence is the thing that is wrong.


Two stale SPDX headers, frozen by a deployment
==============================================

These files carry `// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1`:

  packages/contracts/src/VerdantFactory.sol
  packages/contracts/src/FeeForwarder.sol

They are MIT licensed, like everything else here. The header is a leftover: the
repository was relicensed from BUSL-1.1 to MIT before it was made public, and a
later commit restored these two headers while editing the files for an unrelated
reason.

The obvious fix is not available. An SPDX identifier is part of solc's metadata,
the metadata hash is appended to the compiled bytecode, and both of these files
are compiled into contracts deployed on Robinhood Chain and verified byte-for-byte
on Blockscout:

  VerdantFactory       0x661A5B2A8d7DC0EaEd98B335e070478b40B92Dd9
  FeeForwarderFactory  (embeds FeeForwarder's creation code)

Correcting either header changes that contract's bytecode. The deployment would
no longer be reproducible from this source, and "the deployed code is the source
in this repository" would stop being true — which is a more valuable claim than a
tidy header.

So the grant is stated here instead, and it governs:

  The copyright holder licenses packages/contracts/src/VerdantFactory.sol and
  packages/contracts/src/FeeForwarder.sol under the MIT License in LICENSE,
  notwithstanding the BUSL-1.1 identifier in their headers. No Business Source
  License terms apply to any file in this repository. There is no change date,
  no additional use grant, and no restriction on redeployment.

The headers will be corrected in the same change that next redeploys those
contracts, and not before. `pnpm verify:licenses` enforces both halves of this:
no other file may carry a non-MIT header, and these two may not be "fixed"
without the deployment being redone. See
docs/decisions/013-the-repository-is-mit.md.

The Solidity dependencies are not distributed here. `packages/contracts/vendor/`
holds Uniswap's v4-core, v4-periphery, OpenZeppelin, Solmate and forge-std,
fetched at pinned commits by `scripts/vendor-contracts-deps.sh` and gitignored —
39 MB that never enters version control. Each of those projects carries its own
licence, which travels with it.

`packages/contracts/test/utils/HookMiner.sol` is Uniswap's, under its own MIT
licence, and is the one third-party file committed here rather than fetched. Its
original header is intact.

The typeface is Inter Tight, served from this origin by `next/font` and licensed
under the SIL Open Font License.
